  "title": "Final Parking Space: 1969 Chevrolet Chevy-Van",
  "summary": "During the 1960s, each of the Detroit Big Three offered a line of forward-control compact vans. These sturdy, simple machines became icons of their era and became very popular recipients of the custom-van treatment during the following decade. Of the three, the GM-built version is the hardest to find today. I spotted this half-ton Chevy […]",
